Let Settings -> Repository variables rename a stored variable.

A stored variable's name was read-only, so renaming one meant removing it and
typing its value again under the new name. Now its name is editable like a
new one's. Left blank, its value field still keeps the stored value, which
moves to the new name: saving sends the new name with null in variables, and
renamed maps it to the name it had, so PUT /v1/repo-env
(images/server/omnigent_repo_env_api.py) copies the value inside the Secret
and it never reaches the browser. A typed value replaces it as before.

Under a renamed row, "Renamed from OLD, keeping its value." says so. A stored
variable whose name is cleared asks for a name instead of quietly going; its
x button still removes it. renamed is only sent when something is renamed,
so a save without one is unchanged.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0001-0042.
